    <briefdescription>
<para>A type-checked pair of {<ref refid="classllvm_1_1_register" kindref="compound">Register</ref> Location (or 0), Index}, used to index into a VarLocMap. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This can be efficiently converted to a 64-bit int for insertion into a <ref refid="namespaceanonymous__namespace_02_var_loc_based_impl_8cpp_03_1a0fcac79d5789c3482f72fdb2eb8d0a32" kindref="member">VarLocSet</ref>, and efficiently converted back. The type-checker helps ensure that the conversions aren&apos;t lossy.</para>
<para>Why encode a location /into/ the VarLocMap index? This makes it possible to find the open VarLocs killed by a register def very quickly. This is a performance-critical operation for <ref refid="namespace_live_debug_values" kindref="compound">LiveDebugValues</ref>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
